UPDATE companies SET description='Oregon Made Plastic Products, Inc. (OMPP) was founded in 2011 in Canby, Oregon, by a team with a few product ideas and deep molding know‑how.

Today OMPP operates seven injection molding machines ranging from 25 to 90 tons (with experience up to 150 tons), specializing in small‑part and short‑run production. The shop offers in‑house pad printing, sonic welding, tooling, prototyping, CNC milling, and full mold design and sourcing. It works with both local and offshore mold makers and automation partners to handle projects from concept through production.

The company serves aerospace, automotive, medical, industrial, and electrical sectors. Its customers include manufacturers seeking alternatives to long overseas lead times, entrepreneurs needing a domestic molder, and other molders looking for overflow or specialty capacity.

OMPP emphasizes a quality‑first, low‑cost approach with flexibility to meet varied demand. Sustainability is a stated priority: the firm designs its own products to incorporate regrinds and reprocessed materials, and its tree logo reflects a commitment to reducing plastic waste. When a job falls outside its capabilities, OMPP refers customers to other molders in the region.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Small-part injection molding", "Pad printing", "Sonic welding", "Tooling", "In-house repair and maintenance", "Prototyping", "Machining", "CNC milling", "Part design assistance", "Mold design and sourcing"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Automotive", "Medical", "Industrial", "Electrical"], "materials": ["Various plastics", "Regrinds and reprocessed plastics"], "equipment": ["7 injection molding machines (25\u201390 ton)", "Injection molding machines up to 150 ton"], "volume": "Short run production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quality-first, low-cost shop with flexible scheduling", "Sustainability focus using regrinds and reprocessed materials", "In-house pad printing and sonic welding", "Full mold design and sourcing management", "Referral network with local molders for out-of-scope work"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2011 -> db", "Headquarters Canby, Oregon -> db", "HITCH-GEAR product line launched 2013 -> /", "Sustainability focus using regrinds -> /", "Machine sizes 25-150 ton -> /", "7 molding machines 25-90 tons -> /services", "In-house pad printing and sonic welding -> /, /services", "Industries served: Aerospace, Automotive, Medical, Industrial, Electrical -> /services", "Capabilities: tooling, prototyping, machining, CNC milling, part design assistance, mold design and sourcing -> /services", "Work with local and offshore mold makers and automation -> /", "Short run production specialization -> /, db", "Quality first, efficient, low cost shop -> /", "Tree logo environmental message -> /", "Referral to other molders -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Plastic Injection Molding", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='oregon-made-plastic-products-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Oregon Wire was established in 1973 in Portland, Oregon, as an American manufacturer of wire products and agricultural solutions. The company has operated from its Portland base for over five decades, building a reputation for honesty and integrity in the steel wire supply industry.

The company produces a range of wire products including custom wire forms, trellis systems for commercial growers, baling wire for recycling operations, wire mesh and reinforcement products for construction, and wreath frames, floral wire, and garden supports for the wreath and garden market. Oregon Wire operates a manufacturing facility in Portland and maintains a network of custom wire form manufacturers to fulfill specialized projects. Specific facility size, headcount, and annual volume figures are not publicly disclosed.

Oregon Wire serves commercial growers, recycling facilities, construction contractors, industrial manufacturers, and both professional and hobbyist customers in the wreath and garden segment. The company supplies trellis systems and plant supports to growers, galvanized and black annealed baling wire to recycling operations, and durable wire mesh to construction projects. Its industrial wire solutions address manufacturing and packaging needs.

The company emphasizes flexibility, offering small-quantity orders, local pickup, warehouse services, and extended payment terms. It prioritizes locally sourced, American-made steel and recycled materials, and its customer service team provides updates on inventory, production schedules, and deliveries. Oregon Wire cites its decades of supply chain expertise as a differentiator, helping customers with cost control and inventory management.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wire forms", "Trellis systems", "Baling wire", "Wire mesh", "Reinforcement products", "Wreath frames", "Floral wire", "Garden supports", "Custom fabrication"], "industries": ["Commercial growers", "Recycling", "Construction", "Industrial", "Wreath & Garden"], "materials": ["Steel wire", "Galvanized wire", "Black annealed wire", "Recycled materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Small quantities, local pick-up, warehouse services, and extended terms", "Locally sourced, American-made steel and recycled materials", "Decades of steel wire supply chain expertise", "Customer service team provides real-time updates on inventory, production, and delivery"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1973 -> /about", "Headquarters Portland, Oregon -> /about and db", "Products: custom wire forms, trellis systems, baling wire, wire mesh, reinforcement products, wreath frames, floral wire, garden supports -> /about", "Industries served: commercial growers, recycling, construction, industrial, wreath & garden -> /about", "Flexibility: small quantities, local pick-up, warehouse services, extended terms -> /about", "Sustainability: locally sourced American-made steel, recycled materials -> /about", "Customer service: updates on inventory, production schedules, delivery -> /about", "Manufacturer and supplier -> / (home page)", "Facebook presence -> / (home page)"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Establi