UPDATE companies SET description='Owen Steel Company was founded in 1936 in Columbia, South Carolina, and has since grown from a regional fabricator into a major structural steel contractor with fabrication plants in Columbia, SC, and Wilmington, DE. The company is headquartered in Wilmington, Delaware.

The company provides end-to-end structural steel services, including sales and contracting, project management, engineering and detailing, fabrication, quality assurance, and procurement. Its Columbia facility spans over 440,000 square feet under cranes on a 27-acre site, with single-piece lifting capacity exceeding 70 tons. A second plant in Wilmington, DE, serves the Mid-Atlantic and New York markets. All phases—estimating, engineering, procurement, fabrication, and delivery—are managed in-house by a dedicated project delivery team.

Recent projects include the NYU Langone Medical Center Energy Building, Bronx Criminal Courthouse, John Jay College, Temple University, USC Darla Moore School of Business, VA Hospital in Detroit, World Trade Center Memorial & Museum, Washington D.C. Convention Center, and the West Virginia Meadow River Bridge.

The firm emphasizes its integrated approach—fewer handoffs, early problem-solving, and single-point accountability—as a key differentiator. It holds AISC certifications for Standard Steel Building Structures and Major Steel Bridges with Fracture Critical and Sophisticated Paint Endorsements, and maintains a quality program designed to ensure steel arrives at the project site correct and on schedule.', certifications=ARRAY['AISC Standard Steel Building Structures','AISC Major Steel Bridges','AISC Fracture Critical Endorsement','AISC Sophisticated Paint Endorsement']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Engineering and detailing", "Connection design", "Project management", "Procurement", "Quality assurance (AISC certified)", "Sales and contracting"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Education", "Transportation", "Government", "Commercial construction", "Industrial", "Infrastructure"], "materials": ["Structural steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated in-house team handling engineering, detailing, procurement, fabrication, and delivery", "One of the largest fabrication facilities in the eastern U.S. (440,000+ sq ft, 70+ ton lifting capacity)", "AISC certified for Standard Steel Building Structures, Major Steel Bridges, Fracture Critical, and Sophisticated Paint Endorsements", "Strategically located plants in Columbia, SC, and Wilmington, DE", "Licensed professional engineers developing connections for complex geometry and tight tolerances"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1936 in Columbia, SC -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Wilmington, DE -> db", "Two fabrication plants: Columbia, SC (440,000+ sq ft, 27 acres, 70+ ton lift) and Wilmington, DE -> /services", "Integrated in-house engineering, detailing, procurement, fabrication, delivery -> /services", "AISC certifications: Standard Steel Building Structures, Major Steel Bridges, Fracture Critical, Sophisticated Paint Endorsements -> /services", "Projects include NYU Langone Medical Center, Bronx Criminal Courthouse, John Jay College, Temple University, USC Darla Moore School of Business, VA Hospital Detroit, World Trade Center Memorial, Washington D.C. Convention Center, West Virginia Meadow River Bridge -> /", "Licensed PEs develop connections for complex geometry -> /services", "Worldwide supplier relationships for procurement -> /services", "Dedicated project managers -> /services", "Early engagement in sales and contracting -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Owen Steel brings 90 years of fabrication experience, one of the largest plants in the eastern United States in Columbia, SC, and a second plant in Wilmington, DE, and a fully integrated project team to every contract we take on.", "founded_year": "1936", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='owen-steel-company-fabrication-de' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Owen Suter''s Fine Furniture was founded in 1986 by Richmond native Owen Suter in Richmond, Virginia.

The firm handcrafts neo-classical Americana furniture using time-honored construction techniques and solid hardwoods such as cherry, mahogany, and walnut. The operation emphasizes quality over quantity, with no publicly disclosed headcount or volume metrics.

The company serves residential customers directly through its showroom and online store, providing beds (low-post and poster styles), dining tables, and other heirloom pieces. Testimonials reference buyers from Virginia, Ohio, Georgia, and New York, illustrating a national reach despite the local production base.

