UPDATE companies SET description='Plasteel, a Plastic Engineering Company, operates from Tempe, Arizona. Founded as a woman-owned small business, the company holds ISO 9001:2015 and AS9100 Rev D certifications. It specializes in precision CNC machining of both plastic and metal components, plastic fabrication, and lean/5S shadowboards for tool control.

The 13,200-square-foot facility houses a range of equipment including 5-axis Mazak machining centers, HAAS vertical mills, Doosan turning centers with live tooling and sub-spindles, and large-format Anderson America and C.R. Onsrud CNC routers. With a staff of 50-plus, the shop handles CNC milling, turning, routing, plastic fabrication, FOD tool control, and custom shadowboard and Creform assembly services. Injection molding and vacuum forming are sourced through partner locations.

Plasteel serves aerospace, defense, semiconductor, and medical industries, producing components such as cleanroom fixtures, chemical tanks, water enclosures, and retail displays. The company is ITAR registered and participates in GIDEP, supporting customers with NAICS codes covering aerospace manufacturing, semiconductor machinery, and medical device production.

The company emphasizes quality, 5-axis capability, combined plastic and metal machining, fabrication expertise, and foreign object damage (FOD) control as key differentiators. Its mission focuses on partnership with customers, employees, and the community, aiming to become a regionally recognized brand in machining, fabrication, and lean tool control products.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','GIDEP','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC milling (5-axis and 3-axis)", "CNC turning with live tooling and sub-spindle", "CNC routing (large format)", "Plastic fabrication", "FOD tool control", "Lean/5S shadowboard manufacturing", "SKB case integration", "Creform assembly", "Inspection (CMM, optical comparators, profilometry, microscopy)", "Precision machining of plastic and metal components"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Semiconductor", "Medical"], "materials": ["Plastics", "Metals"], "equipment": ["Mazak VC-500a 5-axis", "Mazak Variaxis C-600 5-axis", "HAAS VF6", "HAAS VF4", "Kent KVR-4020A", "Bridgeport manual mill with power feed and DRO", "ATrump manual mill with power feed and DRO", "Mazak Quick Turn 350MY turning center", "Doosan Puma 2100SY turning center with sub-spindle Y-axis", "Doosan Lynx 220LM lathes", "Doosan Puma GT2100M lathe", "Doosan Puma 2240M lathe", "HAAS SL20T CNC lathe with live tooling", "HAAS SL30 CNC lathe", "Hardinge precision tool room lathe", "Anderson America STRATOS/NEST CNC router 60\" x 120\"", "C.R. Onsrud MSeries CNC router 61\" x 145\"", "MicroView 3-D Automated Imaging", "Suburban Tool Masterview Comparator with DRO", "Mitutoyo PH-3500 Comparator with DRO", "Tesam Micro-hite 3D CMM", "Mahr Pocket Surf 3 Digital Profilometer", "Olympus SZ30 Optical Microscope with illuminator"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 and AS9100 Rev D certified quality system", "5-axis CNC machining for complex plastic and metal parts", "In-house plastic fabrication and FOD tool control solutions", "ITAR registered and GIDEP participant", "Woman-owned small business with 50+ employees"], "facts_used": ["Woman-owned small business -> /", "ISO9001:2015 and AS9100 Rev D certified -> /", "Precision CNC machining of plastic and metal components -> /", "Plastic fabrication and lean/5S shadowboards -> /", "Industries: Aerospace, Defense, Semiconductor, Medical -> /", "Facility: 13,200 sq ft, 50+ employees -> /about-us", "Equipment: Mazak 5-axis, HAAS, Doosan, Anderson America routers -> /", "ITAR registered, GIDEP participant -> /about-us", "CAGE code 58L32 -> /", "Mission: partnership, regional brand in machining, fabrication, lean tool control -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "PlaSteel is an innovative, woman-owned plastic and metal contract manufacturing company", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "50+", "cage_code": "58L32", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Woman-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='plasteel-a-plastic-engineering-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Plastic Molded Concepts (PMC) operates from Eagle, Wisconsin, where it was founded in 1976. The company has spent nearly five decades developing injection molding expertise, focusing on engineered resins for mission-critical components.

PMC specializes in plastic injection molding of engineered resins, offering services that span mold design, consulting, failure analysis, overmolding, insert molding, plastic welding, post-molding operations, in-mold decoration, precision CNC machining, and 3D printing. The company reports having helped customers develop and launch more than 10,000 molded products, supported by in-house Master Molders and state-of-the-art technologies.

The company serves aerospace and defense, medical, filtration, electronics, food and beverage, and automation industries. Its capabilities are tailored for applications requiring complicated part geometry, exotic engineered resins, and tight dimensional tolerances, including insert molding for electronics and medical devices.

PMC differentiates itself as one of the few injection molders specializing in engineered resins, emphasizing its ability to troubleshoot and resolve molding issues that other suppliers cannot. The firm highlights its pre- and post-molding operations and a focus on zero-defect design processes.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Plastic overmolding", "Insert molding", "Plastic welding", "Post-molding operations", "Mold design", "Injection molding consulting", "Failure analysis", "New product design and development", "3D printing", "In-mold decoration", "Precision CNC machining"], "industries": ["Aerospace and Defense", "Medical", "Filtration", "Electronics", "Food and Beverage", "Automation"], "materials": ["Polyethylene", "Engineered resins"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Specializes in molding engineered resins, including exotic grades", "In-house Master Molders and state-of-the-art technologies", "Analysis, troubleshooting, and resolution for molding issues other companies failed to solve", "Pre- and post-molding operations: overmolding, in-mold decoration, precision CNC machining, plastic welding", "10,000+ molded products developed and launched for customers"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1976 -> db", "Headquarters in Eagle, Wisconsin -> db", "Specializes in molding engineered resins -> /", "Offers plastic injection molding, overmolding, insert molding, plastic welding, post-molding operations, mold design, consulting, failure analysis, 3D printing, in-mold decoration, precision CNC machining -> /", "Has helped develop and launch 10,000+ molded products -> /", "Serves aerospace and defense, medical, filtration, electronics, food and beverage, automation industries -> /", "Differentiates as one of few molders specializing in engineered resins with troubleshooting expertise -> /", "In-house Master Molders and state-of-the-art technologies -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are Plastic Molded Concepts (PMC), one of the few plastic injection molding companies in the world that specializes in molding engineered resins.", "founded_year": "1976", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pmc-plastic-molded-concepts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='POET Bioprocessing – Mitchell is a bioprocessing facility operated by POET, LLC, headquartered in Sioux Falls, South Dakota. The company was founded in 1987 with a single facility in Scotland, South Dakota, and has since grown to 35 bioprocessing plants across the Midwest. The Mitchell location began startup in December 2006 and employs approximately 50 team members.

The facility processes roughly 27 million bushels of corn annually to produce 86 million gallons of bioethanol, along with a suite of co-products including dried distillers grains, wet distillers grains, distillers corn oil, condensed distillers solubles (syrup), and pelletized feed products.

Primary markets include fuel blenders for bioethanol, livestock and poultry feed manufacturers for distillers grains and corn oil, and industrial users such as biodiesel producers, ink and paint formulators. The plant partners with over 30,000 local farmers to secure corn supply and supports rural economies through community impact grants.

POET emphasizes an integrated business model that combines research and development with design, construction, technology, operations, public affairs, and marketing. The company states its mission is to produce American-made, plant-based fuel that reduces dependence on oil while strengthening grain markets across the Corn Belt.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Corn milling", "Fermentation", "Distillation", "Dehydration", "Centrifugation", "Drying (distillers grains)", "Pelletizing", "Corn oil extraction", "Transportation logistics", "Bioprocessing facility operations"], "industries": ["Biofuel", "Animal feed", "Biodiesel", "Industrial chemicals (inks, paints)", "Agriculture"], "materials": ["Corn"], "equipment": [], "volume": "86 million gallons bioethanol annually (Mitchell facility); 27 million bushels corn processed annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated R&D, design, construction, technology, operations, and marketing model", "World\u2019s largest biofuel producer and global leader in sustainable bioproducts", "Safe, dependable, cost-effective transportation logistics", "Partnerships with 30,000+ local farmers for reliable corn markets", "Community impact grants supporting local projects"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1987 -> db", "Headquarters Sioux Falls, SD -> db", "35 bioprocessing facilities -> db", "2,600 team members -> db", "Mitchell facility startup December 2006 -> /", "Mitchell facility employs ~50 -> /", "Corn purchased 27M bushels annually -> /", "Bioethanol production 86M gallons annually -> /", "Products: bioethanol, dried distillers grains, distillers corn oil, syrup, wet distillers grains, pellets & cubes -> /", "Industries: biofuel, animal feed, biodiesel, inks, paints -> /", "Integrated business model description -> db", "Transportation logistics expertise -> db", "Partnership with 30,000+ local farmers -> /", "Community impact grants -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Bioprocessing Facility ... Bioethanol Production - 86M gallons annually", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "2600", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/poet/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='poet-bioprocessing-mitchell' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PSPM Plastic Systems operates from a facility in Lebanon, Pennsylvania. The company does not publish its founding year or ownership details, but its public messaging highlights a long-standing commitment to sustainable manufacturing—recycling process water, using low-energy equipment, and air-conditioning production areas to stabilize conditions and cut overhead—well before environmental concerns became mainstream.

The company provides injection molding, assembly, and decoration services, including in-mold labeling (IML) and sleeve application. Its production lines are robotized and integrate assembly, encasing, vision inspection, and automated packing. An in-house engineering and design department supports eco-design and tooling development, while a quality laboratory equipped with 3D measurement, a dynamometer, and melt-flow index (MFI) testing backs process control. PSPM emphasizes total traceability through computerized logs and a release procedure for every finished-goods batch.

PSPM serves primarily the pharmaceutical and food industries. Its quality and hygiene management system is based on HACCP principles and holds BRC-IOP certification, while also meeting ISO 9001 and Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP) requirements. The system is recognized and regularly audited by large pharmaceutical and food-industry clients.

The company positions itself on the premise that quality and energy savings can coexist. Its differentiators include early adoption of resource-efficient processes, a HACCP-driven contamination-prevention framework, robotized lines that combine multiple secondary operations, and end-to-end digital traceability.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 14001','BRC-IOP','ISO 9001','GMP','HACCP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding", "Assembly", "In-mold labeling (IML)", "Sleeve decoration", "Robotized assembly", "Automated packing", "Vision inspection", "Barcode scanning", "Quality control (HACCP, GMP)", "Traceability systems", "Design and engineering", "Eco-design"], "industries": ["Pharmaceutical", "Food and beverage"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["3D measurement equipment", "Dynamometer", "Melt flow index (MFI) tester", "Robotized assembly lines", "Vision inspection systems", "Barcode scanners"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Water recycling and low-energy equipment adopted before environmental regulations", "HACCP-based quality system with BRC-IOP and ISO 9001 certification", "Robotized lines integrating assembly, vision inspection, and automated packing", "Total product traceability via computerized control logs", "Integrated design office offering eco-design services"], "facts_used": ["Location: Lebanon, Pennsylvania -> /", "Sustainable practices: water recycling, low-energy equipment, air-conditioned processes -> db, /", "Processes: injection molding, assembly, decoration (IML, sleeve) -> /", "Robotized lines with assembly, encasing, vision control, automated packing -> /", "Engineering and design department, eco-design -> /", "Quality system based on HACCP, BRC-IOP certified, meets ISO 9001 and GMP -> /quality", "Industries served: pharmaceutical and food industry clients -> /quality, industries_served", "Laboratory equipment: 3D measurement, dynamometer, MFI -> /quality", "Total traceability via computerized control logs -> /quality", "Certifications: ISO 14001 -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our business Injection molding Assembly Decoration IML Sleeve Quality & Hygiene", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pspm-plastic-system' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PURE Workplace Solutions was founded in 1996 in Topeka, Kansas, as a full-service commercial interiors firm. The company operates regionally across Kansas and Missouri and maintains a national presence through offices in Kansas City, Wichita, Topeka, and Chicago.

As an authorized MillerKnoll dealer, PURE provides office furniture, interior design, and architectural products from brands such as Herman Miller, Knoll, NaughtOne, Muuto, DatesWeiser, Geiger, HON, Kimball, National, SitOnIt, Global, and OFS. Its services encompass space planning and design, product specification and procurement, installation and relocation, and project management. Manufacturer-trained and certified crews handle installations, backed by a nationwide network of union and non-union installers. Project managers coordinate delivery schedules with clients, general contractors, and on-site trades to align with construction timelines.

