UPDATE companies SET description='Pack Manufacturing Co. operates from McMinnville, Tennessee, where it was founded in 1994. The company is owned by James and Leisha Brooks, who bought out the remaining shareholders after James had spent two decades at the helm. The business began as a niche provider of custom material handling equipment and has since expanded multiple times while retaining its original family-oriented values.

The company designs and builds custom material handling systems for horticultural and industrial applications. Its product lines include mixers, potting machines, flat fillers, conveyors, bale breakers, and watering systems, all of which can be integrated into fully automated production lines. The facility has grown through several expansions over 25 years, though specific square footage and headcount are not disclosed.

Pack Manufacturing serves agriculture, horticulture, greenhouse, nursery, lumber, mixing, assembly line, mining, compounding, and automotive sectors. Customers range from growers needing media blending and tray filling to industrial operations requiring custom conveying and processing lines. The company emphasizes a consultative approach, helping clients identify the right automation solution rather than pushing standardized equipment.

