UPDATE companies SET description='Beijing-based Panther Healthcare Medical Equipment Co., Ltd. was founded in 2002 as a subsidiary of ITG Health Technology, which is controlled by Xiamen ITG Group Corp., Ltd. (stock code: 600755), a core enterprise of the Fortune Global 500 conglomerate Xiamen ITG Holding Group. The company positions itself as a provider of intelligent minimally invasive surgical solutions in China.

Panther manufactures a comprehensive portfolio of minimally invasive surgical products, including endoscopic staplers, smart staplers, open staplers, ultrasonic scalpels, disposable fixation devices for hernia repair, polymer clips, trocars, and the Panther Ultraseal system. The company also distributes sutures, hernia meshes, and blood vessel titanium clips produced by third parties, and provides OEM manufacturing for certain products. Its devices serve gastrointestinal, gynecologic, thoracic, and bariatric surgical specialties, and are exported to more than 80 countries, with the firm claiming the top export sales ranking among Chinese surgical stapler brands for ten consecutive years from 2016 to 2025.

The company serves hospitals, surgeons, and distributors worldwide, with noted markets including the United States, Germany, Brazil, India, and South Korea. In addition to product supply, Panther operates the Panther Surgical Academy, which organizes surgical trainings, master classes, and clinical immersions globally.

Panther emphasizes an integrated product offering that combines its own manufactured staplers and energy devices with complementary third-party accessories, aiming to provide a one-stop solution for minimally invasive procedures. The firm also highlights its OEM capabilities and global training initiatives as differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 14001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surgical stapler manufacturing (endoscopic, smart, open)", "Energy-based surgical device manufacturing", "Ultrasonic scalpel manufacturing", "Disposable fixation device manufacturing (hernia repair)", "Polymer clip manufacturing", "Trocar manufacturing", "Panther Ultraseal system manufacturing", "Third-party product distribution (sutures, hernia meshes, titanium clips)", "OEM manufacturing", "Surgical training and education (Panther Surgical Academy)"], "industries": ["Minimally invasive surgery", "Surgical staplers", "Energy-based surgical devices", "Gastrointestinal surgery", "Gynecologic surgery", "Thoracic surgery", "Bariatric surgery", "Hernia repair"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Top export sales among Chinese surgical stapler brands for ten consecutive years (2016\u20132025)", "Products exported to over 80 countries and regions", "Integrated portfolio combining manufactured staplers, energy devices, and third-party accessories", "OEM manufacturing for surgical stapler products", "Global surgical training through Panther Surgical Academy"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2002 as subsidiary of ITG Health Technology -> page \"/\"", "Controlled by Xiamen ITG Group (Fortune Global 500) -> page \"/\"", "Headquartered in Beijing, China (ICP license, phone 8610) -> page \"/\"", "Products exported to 80+ countries -> page \"/\"", "Top export sales ranking 2016-2025 -> page \"/\"", "Product portfolio: staplers, energy devices, ultrasonic scalpels, fixation devices, clips, trocars, Ultraseal -> page \"/\"", "Distributes third-party sutures, hernia meshes, titanium clips -> page \"/\"", "OEM manufacturing -> page \"/\"", "Surgical specialties: gastrointestinal, gynecologic, thoracic, bariatric -> page \"/\"", "Panther Surgical Academy for global training -> page \"/\"", "Certification ISO 14001 -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "manufacture and sell certain products to OEM customers", "founded_year": "2002", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/panter-healthcare/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='panther-healthcare-medical-equipment-co-ltd' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Panah Project was founded in 2019 in Brooklyn, New York, by husband-and-wife team Morteza Saifi and Evgeniya Khromina. The studio''s roots trace back to Nairobi, Kenya, where the pair launched an ethical manufacturing initiative that trained women in local communities to produce luxury-quality garments for international markets, creating more than 50 full-time jobs over five years.

Operating from a single facility at 254 36th Street, the company functions as a design studio and full-service sample factory. Its in-house team handles pattern making, sample making, fabric and trim sourcing, cut-and-sew production, grading, fitting, and draping. The factory focuses on low-minimum-order production for emerging and sustainable brands, while also developing footwear lines through established manufacturing relationships in Europe, Asia, and South America.

Panah Project serves a range of clients including established apparel brands, emerging designers, startups, film and theater productions, footwear labels, and bespoke clients seeking one-of-a-kind pieces such as red-carpet looks. For film and theater, the studio creates bespoke costumes tailored to actor measurements and production timelines; for footwear, it supports development across all major categories with flexible minimums.

The founders cite their Nairobi experience as the foundation for the studio''s values—fair wages, long-term opportunity, and craftsmanship. Morteza Saifi, formerly Executive Creative Director at Camuto Group, leads creative and technical direction, while Evgeniya Khromina guides strategy and operations. The company emphasizes a streamlined, under-one-roof process that maintains quality control from design through to market-ready pieces.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pattern making", "Sample making", "Fabric and trim sourcing", "Cut-and-sew production", "Low-MOQ production", "Design and development", "Grading", "Fitting", "Draping", "Footwear development", "Footwear production", "Costume design", "Costume production", "Bespoke garment construction", "Red-carpet look creation"], "industries": ["Apparel brands", "Emerging designers", "Startups", "Film and theater", "Footwear", "Bespoke/celebrity"], "materials": ["Premium cottons", "Silks", "Sustainable fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low-MOQ and small-batch production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All services under one roof: design, pattern making, sampling, sourcing, and production", "Low-MOQ production in Brooklyn factory", "Extensive sourcing network in Europe and Asia with flexible minimums", "30 years of combined experience in design and development", "Ethical manufacturing heritage from Nairobi initiative creating 50+ jobs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2019 by Morteza Saifi and Evgeniya Khromina -> db", "Headquarters Brooklyn, NY -> db", "Services: pattern making, sample making, sourcing, production, development -> /", "Industries served: brands, emerging designers, startups, film & theater, footwear, bespoke -> /", "Nairobi ethical manufacturing initiative created 50+ jobs -> /", "Morteza Saifi former Executive Creative Director at Camuto Group -> /", "Low-MOQ production in Brooklyn factory -> /", "Sourcing network in Europe and Asia -> /", "Address 254 36th St B-523, Brooklyn, NY 11232 -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Panah Project is a Brooklyn-based sample factory specializing in full-service clothing development.", "founded_year": "2019", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "Low-MOQ", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pan-h-project' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pappas Foods LLC, operating as Lassonde Pappas, is headquartered in Springdale, Arkansas. The company manufactures a range of shelf-stable beverages and food products for distribution across multiple channels of trade.

Its product portfolio includes organic, natural, and conventional shelf-stable juices, ready-to-drink teas, enhanced waters, isotonics, and cranberry sauces. Production takes place in strategically located, state-of-the-art multi-process facilities capable of multi-serve, single-serve, and multi-pack formats. An in-house R&D team supports collaborative innovation and product development, while dedicated food safety, regulatory affairs, and quality assurance groups monitor compliance with customer specifications and regulatory requirements.

The company serves customers through many classes of trade nationwide, supplying retail, foodservice, and other distribution channels. Its business model emphasizes strategic partnerships and continuous communication to build long-term relationships.

