UPDATE companies SET description='Par Hawaii Refining traces its roots to 1904 when The Gas Company was established in Hawaii. Pacific Resources, Inc. (PRI) became the holding company for both the gas utility and the refinery. Today, Par Hawaii is a subsidiary of Par Pacific Holdings (NYSE: PARR), headquartered in Houston, Texas, while its corporate offices remain in Kapolei on Oahu.

The company operates the only petroleum refinery in Hawaii, where 660 employees run 24/7 operations to convert imported crude oil into gasoline, diesel, fuel oil, ship fuel, and aviation fuels including jet fuel. Refined products move through an integrated logistics network of pipelines, tanker trucks, and barges serving all major Hawaiian islands. Par Hawaii also markets fuels through a statewide retail network of Hele, 76, and nomnom-branded stations. The refinery supplies the energy needs of roughly 1.4 million residents and 8 million annual visitors.

Primary customers include electric and gas utilities, major airlines such as Hawaiian Airlines and Alaska Airlines, the U.S. military, and the general public via retail outlets. Par Hawaii has also formed a joint venture with Mitsubishi Corp. and ENEOS Corp. to develop renewable fuels, and is collaborating with Hawaiian Airlines to explore sustainable aviation fuel production by retooling an existing refinery unit.

The company states its mission as "Humbly Serving Communities," emphasizing reliable, safe, and environmentally responsible energy supply for an isolated island state. Leadership cites integrity, creativity, hard work, and respect as core values guiding a transition toward decarbonization, including carbon sequestration and renewable fuel production, to meet Hawaii''s ambitious clean-energy goals.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Petroleum refining", "Fuel distribution (pipeline, truck, barge)", "Retail fuel sales", "Renewable fuel development", "Engineering", "Information technology", "Customer service"], "industries": ["Electric utilities", "Gas utilities", "Aviation", "Marine", "Defense / Military", "Retail fuel"], "materials": ["Crude oil", "Gasoline", "Diesel", "Fuel oil", "Ship fuel", "Aviation fuel", "Jet fuel", "Renewable fuels"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only petroleum refinery in Hawaii", "Foreign-Trade Zone operation since 1972", "24/7 refining operations with integrated pipeline, truck, and barge distribution to all major islands", "Statewide retail network under Hele, 76, and nomnom brands", "Partnerships with Mitsubishi, ENEOS, and Hawaiian Airlines for renewable and sustainable aviation fuels"], "facts_used": ["Founded as The Gas Company in 1904 -> /about-us", "Refinery built in Campbell Industrial Park, Kapolei -> /about-us", "Foreign-Trade Zone since 1972 -> /about-us", "Parent company Par Pacific Holdings (NYSE: PARR) -> /", "Headquarters in Kapolei, Hawaii -> /", "660 employees -> /", "Only petroleum refinery in Hawaii -> /", "Products: gasoline, diesel, fuel oil, ship fuel, aviation fuel -> /", "Logistics: pipelines, tanker trucks, barges -> /", "Retail brands: Hele, 76, nomnom -> /", "Customers: electric/gas utilities, major airlines, US military, public -> /about-us", "Partnership with Mitsubishi and ENEOS for renewable fuels -> /", "Partnership with Hawaiian Airlines for sustainable aviation fuel -> /about-us", "Mission: Humbly Serving Communities -> /about-us", "Values: Integrity, Creativity, Hard work, Respect For Others -> /about-us", "Leadership: Eric Wright, Deaglan McClean, John Peyton -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Par Hawaii operates the only petroleum refinery in the state and distributes fuels via pipelines on Oahu and on barges to all major harbors in the state.", "founded_year": "1904", "employee_count": "660", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='par-hawaii-refining' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Paragon Metal Fabricators was established in 1989 in Erlanger, Kentucky, by brothers Joe, Stan, and Mark Muehlenkamp. After years of planning and market research revealed a strong need for quality metal fabrication in the Cincinnati tri-state area, the three founders combined over 100 years of experience in engineering, sales, and fabrication to launch the business. The company remains family-owned and operated, now led by the second generation—brothers Bryan, Matthew, and Jason Muehlenkamp—who continue the original focus on quality and customer satisfaction.

The shop specializes in sheet metal and structural fabrication, offering flat and tube laser cutting, waterjet cutting, forming, rolling, welding, powder coating, and machining (turning, milling, drilling), along with assembly and finishing. Operations run out of a 42,000-square-foot facility in Erlanger and a new 126,000-square-foot plant in Falmouth, Kentucky, equipped with Bystronic and Cincinnati laser systems, waterjet machines, press brakes, and vertical mills. A team of over 30 employees handles materials from light gauge to heavy plate, supporting prototype work through high-volume production runs.

Paragon serves a diverse industrial base including agriculture, air handling, automotive, consumer products, energy, material handling, mining, construction, and packaging equipment.

The company emphasizes its decades of proven performance, capabilities built to handle difficult jobs, and precision results with efficient delivery. Founders started the business to fill a gap for reliable, quality-focused fabrication, and the second generation maintains that standard with in-house powder coating, certified welders, and a no-minimum-order policy for quotes.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting (flat)", "Tube laser cutting", "Waterjet cutting", "Metal forming (press brake)", "Metal rolling", "Welding (MIG/TIG/stick)", "Powder coating", "CNC machining (turning, milling, drilling)", "Assembly", "Finishing", "Precision machining"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Air Handling", "Automotive", "Consumer Products", "Energy", "Material Handling", "Mining", "Construction", "Packaging Equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Bystronic laser equipment", "Cincinnati laser equipment", "Advanced powder coating line", "Waterjet machines", "Plasma cutting machine", "Press brake", "Vertical milling machines"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned with second-generation leadership", "In-house powder coating line for high-volume, high-precision finishes", "AWS-certified welders and certified laser equipment operators", "Flat and tube laser cutting with Bystronic and Cincinnati systems", "No minimum order; quotes provided for one- and two-piece jobs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 by Joe, Stan, Mark Muehlenkamp -> /about", "Family-owned and operated -> /", "Second-generation ownership: Bryan, Matthew, Jason Muehlenkamp -> /about", "42,000 sq ft facility in Erlanger -> /", "New 126,000 sq ft facility in Falmouth, KY -> /", "Services: laser cutting, tube laser, waterjet, forming, rolling, welding, powder coating, machining, assembly, finishing -> /services", "Industries served: agriculture, air handling, automotive, consumer products, energy, material handling, mining, construction, packaging equipment -> /", "AWS welding certification (Matthew Muehlenkamp) -> /about", "Bystronic and Cincinnati laser equipment certifications -> /about", "Over 30 employees managed by Matthew Muehlenkamp -> /about", "Prototype to full-scale production -> /services", "Competitive quotes on one-piece and two-piece orders -> /", "Focus on quality, custom solutions from design to delivery -> /", "Why Choose Us: Experience, Capabilities, Quality -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializing in sheet metal and structural fabrication", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "30+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='paragon-metal-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Park Manufacturing was founded in 1946 in Cambridge, Minnesota, after an OEM approached the company with a wire harness problem that needed solving.

