UPDATE companies SET description='Parker Medical Associates, LLC operates from Charlotte, North Carolina, where it was founded in 1987 by Bruce Parker. Parker began manufacturing a patented fiberglass roll splinting system that transformed fracture care worldwide.

Today the firm focuses on specialty athletic protective guards and resin‑impregnated fiberglass products, serving as the official manufacturer of the EvoShield® GEL‑TO‑SHELL™ line for Wilson Sporting Goods. Its Charlotte facility provides full‑service cut‑and‑sew operations including sewing, contract cutting, specialty knitting, and packaging and fulfillment. The company also produces signature cut‑and‑sew product lines for a range of other customers.

Wilson Sporting Goods is a named customer for the EvoShield brand, while the company’s membership in the Carolina Textile District and Manufactured in North Carolina reflects its integration into the regional textile supply chain.

Parker Medical emphasizes ethical manufacturing, stating that none of its products contain substances listed under the EU REACH regulation or California Proposition 65. Its mission highlights quality, responsiveness, corporate citizenship, a safe workplace, and long‑term partnerships built on clear implementation plans from design through delivery.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sewing", "Contract Cutting", "Specialty Knitting", "Packaging and Fulfillment", "Resin impregnated fiberglass manufacturing"], "industries": ["Sporting goods", "Medical devices", "Textile manufacturing", "Athletic equipment"], "materials": ["Fiberglass", "Resin", "Gel (GEL-TO-SHELL)", "Textiles"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Official manufacturer of EvoShield\u00ae GEL\u2011TO\u2011SHELL\u2122 products for Wilson Sporting Goods", "REACH and California Prop 65 compliant (no hazardous substances)", "Member of Carolina Textile District and Manufactured in North Carolina", "Full\u2011service cut\u2011and\u2011sew: sewing, contract cutting, specialty knitting, packaging & fulfillment"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1987 by Bruce Parker in Charlotte, NC -> /about-us", "Manufacturer of specialty athletic protective guards and resin impregnated fiberglass-based products -> /about-us", "Official manufacturer of EvoShield GEL-TO-SHELL products for Wilson Sporting Goods -> /about-us", "Services: Sewing, Contract Cutting, Packaging & Fulfillment, Specialty Knitting -> /about-us, /", "Member of Carolina Textile District and Manufactured in North Carolina -> /", "REACH and Prop 65 compliant -> /about-us", "Headquarters at 2400 Distribution St, Charlotte, NC 28203 -> /about-us", "Sold splinting and casting business assets in 2018 -> /about-us", "Mission emphasizes quality, responsiveness, corporate citizenship, safe workplace, long-term partnerships -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "For almost 40 years, Parker Medical Associates, LLC has been a premier manufacturer of specialty athletic protective guards and other resin impregnated fiberglass-based products located in Charlotte, NC.", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='parker-medical-associates-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Parts Midwest, Inc. was founded in 1972 in Mounds View, Minnesota. The company operates as a 100% employee-owned business and is part of the SCIPI Companies family, bringing shared ownership and international reach to its partnerships.

The firm specializes in accessories program management for automotive original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) and their dealership networks. Its services include in-store training, sales call coaching, dealership performance assessments, and dealer engagement reviews, all structured around a proprietary More Accessories Profitability Process (M.A.P.P.). Parts Midwest also functions as a distribution network, managing accessory logistics outside the factory to reduce build complexity for OEMs. The company reports serving over 900 dealerships.

Its primary customers are new vehicle OEMs and their franchised dealerships across the automotive manufacturing sector. A referenced client includes Ford of Canada, where the company supported accessory business development for a decade.

The company states its mission is to simplify complex accessory programs and strengthen every link in the supply chain by aligning strategy with service, enabling OEMs to achieve consistent, measurable success. Its six stated values—do the right thing, families first, ownership, working together, respectful relationships, and fun at work—guide its approach.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Accessories program management", "In-store training", "Sales call training", "Dealership performance assessment", "Dealer engagement review", "Distribution network management", "Accessories integration", "M.A.P.P. process", "CRM reporting", "Process alignment", "Strategy consulting"], "industries": ["Automotive Manufacturing & Their Dealers"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% employee-owned", "Part of SCIPI Companies with international operations", "Serves over 900 dealerships", "Proprietary M.A.P.P. process for accessory profitability", "Operates as distribution network for OEM accessories"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 -> db", "Headquarters Mounds View, Minnesota -> db", "100% employee-owned -> /", "Part of SCIPI Companies -> /", "Serves over 900 dealerships -> /", "M.A.P.P. process -> /", "Distribution network for OEMs -> /", "Client Ford of Canada -> /", "Mission to simplify accessory programs -> /", "Industries: Automotive Manufacturing & Their Dealers -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Beyond service, we also operate as a distribution network for new vehicle OEMs, helping them save costs and reduce build complexity at the factory by managing accessories outside the production line.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='parts-midwest-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1972, Pasco Tool & Plastics Inc. has operated from Meadville, Pennsylvania for over five decades. The company provides tooling, machining, and injection molding services from a 28,000-square-foot, temperature-controlled facility designed to hold close tolerances on critical applications.

Its capabilities span tool design and manufacture, precision machining, and plastic injection molding, supported by a full-service quality control and metrology department. Equipment in that department is calibrated to traceable national standards, and the shop runs first-article inspections with pre-production part approval processes (PPAP) for each project. The facility''s climate control helps maintain dimensional stability across production runs.

The company serves automotive, electronics, military, medical, and safety-product markets. Each project receives personal attention, with professional guidance offered from initial design through final delivery.

Management emphasizes that quality is built into daily routines rather than inspected in at the end. The firm differentiates itself by staying involved throughout the production cycle, offering professional guidance from design approval through final delivery. Teamwork and continuous improvement are cited as core to their quality commitment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Tooling", "Machining", "Injection Molding", "Quality Control / Metrology", "First Article Inspection", "Pre-Production Part Approval Process (PPAP)", "Laboratory Services"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Electronics", "Military", "Medical", "Safety"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-service quality control and metrology department with equipment calibrated to traceable national standards", "First-article inspection and pre-production part approval process (PPAP) on every project", "28,000 sq ft temperature-controlled facility for dimensional stability", "Personal project attention with professional guidance from design through delivery", "Commitment to continuous improvement across all business aspects"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 -> db", "Headquarters Meadville, Pennsylvania -> db", "28,000 sq ft temperature-controlled facility -> /", "Tooling, machining, injection molding services -> /", "Industries: automotive, electronics, military, medical, safety -> /", "Full-service quality control/metrology department with traceable calibration -> /quality", "First article inspection and PPAP -> /quality", "Close tolerances on critical applications -> /", "Personal attention per project -> /", "Professional guidance throughout production -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our business is in tooling, machining, and injection molding.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": 