UPDATE companies SET description='That company later became Performance Food Group (PFG), a Fortune 500 corporation. The Denver division took shape through a series of mergers: Vendor Supply of America (founded 1970 by Alan and Gerald Marcove), Roma Distribution (1955), Donsons Distributing (1957), and Leprino’s restaurant supply division (1994). In 2005, Vistar Corporation and Roma Foods merged to form Roma Denver, which was folded into PFG after Blackstone and Wellspring acquired the group in 2008. Today the business runs as a PFG subsidiary serving the Rocky Mountain region.

The distributor runs a 350,000-square-foot facility staffed by more than 1,000 employees. Its catalog holds 15,000 to 25,000 SKUs, including 3,500 locally sourced items and products from 750 brand partners such as Roma® and West Creek®. A dedicated fleet and logistics network achieve a 98 percent fill rate on customer orders. The PFS Express program adds daily deliveries across Colorado, Wyoming, and New Mexico with late cut-off times and no minimum-order requirement. Customers also use the Customer First Application for 24/7 ordering, tracking, and inventory management.

The company serves independent restaurants, chains, and institutional kitchens throughout Colorado, Wyoming, and New Mexico — roughly 5,000 accounts, 94 percent of which are small businesses.

PFG’s four stated values — Service Excellence, Innovation, Integrity, and Community Support — frame the Denver division’s approach. The business says it was built to solve supply-chain disruptions, labor shortages, and rising costs that threaten menu consistency and profitability for local operators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Foodservice distribution", "Inventory management", "Logistics and delivery", "Customized product sourcing", "Digital ordering platform (Customer First Application)", "Express delivery service (PFS Express)", "Local sourcing programs", "Menu consulting (Culinology)", "Flexible delivery schedules", "Specialized product sourcing", "Real-time delivery tracking", "24/7 online ordering", "Phone ordering support", "Supply chain management", "Product variety (15,000-25,000 SKUs)", "Brand partner management (750+ brands)", "Local producer support (3,500+ items)", "Fill rate optimization (98%)", "Small business partnership programs", "Community support initiatives"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Restaurant industry", "Hospitality", "Independent restaurant operators", "Healthcare foodservice", "Educational institutions", "Quick-service restaurants", "Full-service restaurants"], "materials": ["Roma\u00ae and West Creek\u00ae further processed chicken products", "Locally sourced food items (3,500+)", "Products from 750+ trusted brand partners", "Exclusive brand products (40+ brands)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Daily deliveries with late order cutoffs", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Daily deliveries across Colorado, Wyoming, and New Mexico", "Late order cutoffs for last-minute needs", "No minimum order requirements on PFS Express", "State-of-the-art 350,000 sq. ft. distribution facility", "Customer First Application for 24/7 ordering and real-time tracking"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Henderson, Colorado -> db", "Founded 1885 (Pocahontas Foods) -> /about", "Part of Performance Food Group (Fort