UPDATE companies SET description='Phase Sensitive Innovations (PSI) is a small, high-technology company based in Newark, Delaware, specializing in RF photonic devices, components, and systems with a focus on the millimeter-wave region of the electromagnetic spectrum.

The company designs and manufactures high-speed UTC photodiodes, ultra-high-speed lithium niobate phase modulators (up to 500 GHz), broadband RF photonic links, and tunable optical paired source (TOPS) systems for wideband RF signal synthesis. It provides a full suite of photonic integrated circuit (PIC) capabilities — design, simulation, layout, multi-project wafer submission, and characterization — alongside custom RF design, RF component testing from DC to 1 THz, and RF/optical packaging (flip-chip, wire/ribbon bonding, hermetic sealing). In-house fabrication occupies over 3,000 sq ft of laboratory and cleanroom space, including a 1,200 sq ft ISO Class 6/7 cleanroom for wafer processing up to 6-inch diameter and 1,000+ sq ft for mid- and back-end assembly. The shop also runs a Mazak V500C CNC mill (3-axis and 3D simultaneous) and a 3NTR A2V4 3D printer for multi-material polymer parts.

Its devices enable millimeter-wave imaging for security scanning and vision enhancement, RF-over-fiber links, antenna remoting, phased-array beamforming, and RF surveillance across microwave, millimeter-wave, and terahertz bands.

The company emphasizes its phase-locking upconversion technology, which it says delivers unprecedented beam-bandwidth processing for next-generation 5G and beyond. It also highlights photodiode power handling and linearity, lithium niobate modulators covering the full millimeter-wave spectrum, and an end-to-end PIC design-to-fabrication flow under an ISO 9001:2015 quality system certified by TÜV SÜD.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["RF design and consulting (microwave to 300 GHz)", "UWB phased array antenna design", "High-frequency PCB design and layout", "mmW packaging design", "RF component testing and characterization (DC to 1 THz)", "Anechoic chamber far-field measurement", "Time domain analysis (TDA)", "S-parameter measurements beyond 1 THz", "Dielectric constant / loss tangent measurement", "Photonic integrated circuit (PIC) design and simulation", "PIC schematic and physical layout", "Multi-project wafer (MPW) submission", "Photonic device and component testing (die-level and packaged)", "Custom photonic device design and fabrication", "RF and optical packaging and integration", "Flip-chip bonding", "Wire bonding and ribbon bonding", "Hermetic packaging", "Wafer and chip dicing", "Environmental stress testing (vibration, thermal cycling)", "High-precision CNC machining (3-axis and 3D simultaneous)", "3D printing (hard plastics, elastic plastics, high-strength polymers)", "Laser engraving"], "industries": ["Defense", "Industrial", "5G / 6G Cellular", "Radar", "Satellite", "Security", "Communications", "Vision Enhancement", "Millimeter Wave Imaging", "RF-over-Fiber", "Antenna Remoting", "Security Scanning", "RF Surveillance", "Phased Array Antenna Systems"], "materials": ["Lithium Niobate"], "equipment": ["Mazak V500C CNC mill", "3NTR A2V4 3D printer (triple extruder)", "RMI Fiber Laser Engraving System"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Phase-locking upconversion technology for beam-bandwidth processing in 5G/B5G", "High-speed UTC photodiodes with world-leading power handling and linearity", "Lithium niobate phase modulators operating up to 500 GHz", "Full in-house PIC design, simulation, layout, MPW submission, and characterization", "ISO 9001:2015 quality management system certified by T\u00dcV S\u00dcD"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Newark, Delaware -> db", "Specializes in RF photonic devices for 5G, RF-over-fiber, antenna remoting -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified by T\u00dcV S\u00dcD -> /about", "Over 3000 sqft cleanroom and lab space -> /", "CNC milling (Mazak V500C) and 3D printing (3NTR A2V4) in-house -> /services", "Industries served: Defense, Industrial, 5G, Radar, Satellite, Security -> /services", "Custom photonic device design and fabrication with 1200 sqft ISO 6/7 cleanroom -> /services", "RF testing up to 1 THz -> /services", "Lithium Niobate phase modulators up to 500 GHz -> /", "High-speed UTC photodiodes with world-leading power handling -> /", "Phase-locking upconversion technology for beam-bandwidth processing -> /", "Full suite of PIC design, simulation, layout, MPW submission -> /services", "RF and optical packaging: flip-chip, wire-bonding, hermetic packaging -> /services", "3D printing with hard plastics, elastic plastics, high-strength polymers -> /services", "Laser engraving with RMI Fiber Laser Engraving System -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Phase Sensitive Innovations (PSI) specializes in creating and incorporating photonic devices into various RF systems, including 5G wireless communication, high bandwidth RF-over-fiber, and antenna remoting.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='phase-sensitive-innovations' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Piedmont Electrical Distributors of Greenville, Inc. was founded in 1985 in Greenville, South Carolina, by Tim Franke and his partner with the goal of becoming the electrical supplier for the region''s construction and industrial markets. The business remains family-owned; Tim and his wife Francine led the company for years before their son Josh Franke took over as owner.

The company operates a 36,000-square-foot warehouse stocking a broad range of electrical products including circuit breakers, lighting fixtures, conduit, and wire. It serves customers across South Carolina, North Carolina, and Georgia through both delivery and a counter service for immediate pick-up. When items are not in stock, the team sources them quickly to minimize project downtime.

Piedmont Electrical primarily serves contractors and industrial facilities in the Upstate region. Its customer base includes on-site superintendents, electrical contractors, and industrial maintenance teams who rely on the distributor for timely material delivery and responsive communication. Testimonials from field supervisors highlight the company''s willingness to deliver to job sites over an hour away and to accommodate last-minute order changes.

