UPDATE companies SET description='Plastipak Packaging Inc. was founded in 1967 in Champaign, Illinois, by Bill Young, who joined his family''s water delivery business after graduating from the University of Detroit.

Today Plastipak operates as a global manufacturer of rigid plastic packaging and recycling solutions, with more than 50 production sites across North America, South America, Europe, Africa, and Asia. Its core processes include extrusion blow molding, injection stretch blow molding (ISBM), PET and ePET molding, wide-mouth container technology, hot-fill and barrier container engineering, decoration (embossing, debossing, direct-object printing), and the production of both virgin and post-consumer recycled (PCR) resins. The company holds over 500 U.S. patents and more than 1,000 international patents, reflecting a portfolio of proprietary systems such as the rotary dual-cavity ISBM machine, the 30-station G.E.M. PAK extrusion wheel, and recent innovations like SprayPET Revolution™ aerosol packaging, PPK Natura™ carbon-waste PET resin, and O2blox™ nylon-free oxygen barrier.

Plastipak serves a broad range of end markets, including carbonated and non-carbonated beverages, hot-fill juices and teas, beer, UHT milk, dairy, household and commercial products (detergents, personal care), automotive, industrial, and agricultural chemicals. Long-standing customers have included Pepsi, Kraft, Heineken, Downy Unstopables, and Hilltop Honey, illustrating the company''s reach across multinational brands and regional producers alike.

Plastipak differentiates itself through vertical integration (in-house resin production, mold design, recycling via its Clean Tech centers), a global footprint that enables local service, and a sustained investment in circular-economy technologies that turn post-consumer waste into new packaging.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Extrusion blow molding", "Injection stretch blow molding (ISBM)", "PET molding", "ePET molding", "Wide-mouth container technology", "Hot-fill container engineering", "Barrier container technology (carbon-coated, nylon-free O2blox)", "Decoration: embossing, debossing, direct-object printing", "Post-consumer recycled (PCR) resin production", "Virgin resin manufacturing", "Plastic recycling (Clean Tech centers)", "Aerosol packaging (SprayPET Revolution)", "Multi-layer HDPE container molding", "Rotary dual-cavity ISBM system", "G.E.M. PAK extrusion wheel system"], "industries": ["Beverage (carbonated, non-carbonated water, hot-fill, beer, UHT milk)", "Dairy", "Household & commercial (detergents, personal care)", "Automotive", "Industrial", "Agricultural", "Food (ambient, salad dressing)", "Personal care"], "materials": ["PET", "ePET", "HDPE", "rHDPE (post-consumer recycled HDPE)", "PCR resin (rPET)", "Virgin resin", "Carbon-waste PET (PPK Natura)", "Nylon-free PET (O2blox)"], "equipment": ["Rotary dual-cavity ISBM blow molding system", "30-station G.E.M. PAK extrusion wheel system", "Clean Tech plastic recycling center", "Solar-powered recycling center (Toledo, Spain)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house resin production, mold design, and recycling via Clean Tech centers", "Over 500 U.S. patents and 1,000+ international patents protecting proprietary technologies", "Global network of 50+ manufacturing sites across five continents", "Circular-economy innovations: PCR resin, carbon-waste PET (PPK Natura\u2122), nylon-free barrier (O2blox\u2122)", "Proprietary molding systems: rotar