UPDATE companies SET description='Podiumwear Custom Sports Apparel was founded in 2003 in St. Paul, Minnesota, by Reid Lutter, a nordic ski racer and coach with four decades of trail experience. Frustrated by the difficulties of ordering custom uniforms for his own teams, Lutter set out to build a company that would make the process enjoyable and stress‑free, starting with nordic ski apparel before expanding into cycling, running, and soccer.

The company produces fully custom team uniforms and apparel — jerseys, tops, shorts, training jackets, pants, and socks — for a wide range of sports including cycling, nordic skiing, running, soccer, volleyball, football, basketball, hockey, lacrosse, clay target sports, softball, baseball, mountain biking, cross‑country, and track and field. Customers work one‑on‑one with designers or use an online customizer, and orders can be shipped directly to each athlete or to a single team contact. A partnership with The North Face and U.S. Ski & Snowboard adds a high‑profile dimension to its nordic program.

Podiumwear serves youth, club, and school teams across the United States and internationally. Its customers include team uniform directors, coaches, administrators, and parents who need reliable, on‑time delivery for seasonal competition. The company highlights testimonials from a team uniform director, a team administrator, and a club parent, underscoring its focus on easing the administrative burden of uniform procurement.

Lutter’s original goal — concierge‑level service, fast turnaround, and top‑tier quality — remains the stated differentiator. Podiumwear emphasizes total design freedom without templates, durability that lasts multiple seasons, and a policy that allows two below‑minimum re‑orders per calendar year to accommodate roster changes.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom apparel design", "Online jersey customizer", "Team store management", "Direct-to-individual shipping", "Below-minimum re-order program"], "industries": ["Cycling", "Nordic skiing", "Running", "Soccer", "Volleyball", "Football", "Basketball", "Hockey", "Lacrosse", "Clay target sports", "Softball", "Baseball", "Mountain biking", "Cross-country", "Track and field"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Concierge-level customer service", "Fast turnaround times", "Total design freedom with no templates", "Direct shipping to individual team members", "Two below-minimum re-orders allowed per year"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2003 -> db", "Headquarters in St. Paul, Minnesota -> db", "Founder Reid Lutter, CEO -> /about", "Started with nordic skiing, expanded to cycling, running, soccer -> /about", "Offers custom team uniforms for 15+ sports -> /", "Partnership with The North Face and US Ski and Snowboard -> /", "Concierge-level customer service, fast turnaround, top-tier quality -> /about", "Total design freedom, no templates -> /", "Direct shipping to individuals or single contact -> /", "Two below-minimum re-orders per calendar year -> db (products)", "Uses best materials for durability -> /", "Testimonials from Team Uniform Director, Team Administrator, Club Parent -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Podiumwear has redefined what it means to create custom uniforms", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='podiumwear-custom-sports-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Point Medical Corporation operates from Crown Point, Indiana, where it develops and fabricates implant-grade silicone rubber devices and assemblies for medical applications. The company focuses on custom development and fabrication to meet exacting tolerances and specifications required in the medical environment.

The facility is FDA-registered and ISO 13485:2016 certified, with a Class 10,000 clean room. In-house prototype development and tooling accelerate the transition to production. Capabilities span extrusion (custom, multi-lumen, co-extrusion, miniature profiles, wire-reinforced, striped, close-tolerance, translucent, radiopaque), catheter assembly (smooth transition tube-to-lumen molding, balloons, coil forming, printing, complete fabrication, latex-to-silicone conversion), molding (liquid injection, top transfer, compression, insert), and tipping (forming, clean-cut holes, step cutting, taper and bullet tips).

Point Medical serves medical device manufacturers and clinical consultants, providing custom silicone rubber components for applications such as catheters, tubing, and implantable assemblies. The company also operates Martech Medical Products for non-silicone plastics manufacturing.

