ent, radiopaque, tubing cut lengths or coils -> /capabilities", "Catheter assembly capabilities: smooth transition tube-to-lumen molding, balloons, coil forming, printing, complete catheter fabrication, conversion from latex to silicone -> /capabilities", "Molding capabilities: liquid injection molding (LIM), top transfer molding, compression molding, insert molding -> /capabilities", "Tipping capabilities: forming, clean-cut holes and eyelets, step cutting, one-piece smooth transition taper or bullet tips -> /capabilities", "Works closely with customers and clinical consultants -> /", "Customer commitment extends to ongoing inquiry into latest technology, materials, and manufacturing methods -> /capabilities", "Reputation for superior quality and innovative design from consistent attention to materials, machining and manufacturing techniques -> /", "Martech Medical Products for plastics manufacturing other than silicone -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Point Medical specializes in the custom development and fabrication of implant grade silicone rubber devices and assemblies", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='point-medical-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Poly-Ject Inc. was founded in 1982 in Amherst, New Hampshire. The company began as a custom plastic injection molding operation and has grown into a full-service provider of design, rapid prototyping, mold making, and injection molding.

Operating from a 26,000-square-foot facility in Amherst, Poly-Ject runs injection molding production 24 hours a day, five days a week. The company maintains in-house mold-making and engineering design capabilities, allowing it to handle projects from concept through production. Services include plastic injection molding, custom molding, rapid prototyping, and mold making.

Poly-Ject serves customers across New England and the broader United States, providing plastic components for a range of applications.

The company emphasizes domestic production as an alternative to offshore sourcing, citing quality and price competitiveness. Its ISO 9000 certification and policy of not shipping parts that fail quality checks underscore a focus on consistency.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9000']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Custom plastic injection molding", "Mold making", "Rapid prototyping", "Engineering design"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["26,000 sq ft facility in Amherst, NH", "24/5 production schedule", "In-house mold making and design", "ISO 9000 certified quality system", "Domestic production alternative to offshore sourcing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 -> db", "Headquarters Amherst, NH -> db", "26,000 sq ft facility -> /", "24/5 production schedule -> /", "In-house mold making and design capabilities -> /", "ISO 9000 certification -> /", "Services: Engineering, Rapid Prototyping, Mold Making, Injection Molding -> /", "Serving New England and United States -> /", "No offshore outsourcing claim -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Poly-Ject Inc. will design and manufacture your plastic parts to exacting specifications.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='poly-ject-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Port Erie Plastics was founded in 1953 in Harborcreek, Pennsylvania, and remains a family-owned, engineering-driven manufacturer.

The company specializes in custom plastic injection molding and structural foam injection molding for large components, with wall thicknesses from 0.200 to 0.500 inches and part lengths up to 7.5 feet. Its facility runs nearly 90 injection molding machines in a 24/7 production environment, supported by a full-service in-house tool room that handles mold building, refurbishment, and maintenance. Port Erie also manages structured tool transfers and validation, often bringing transferred molds into steady production within days.

Port Erie serves OEMs across consumer products, office furniture, durable goods, building materials, home improvement, kitchen and appliance components, electronic housings, material handling, lawn and garden, and building and construction. Past programs include structural foam redesign of HDPE trench drains for the construction industry, injection molding of polypropylene and elastomer lids for cookware, and development of combination dials for safe manufacturing. The company also supported an urgent medical product mold transfer that restored production in a single weekend.

The company says its differentiation lies in disciplined tooling control, process validation, and a project engineer assigned to each program for technical ownership from quote through full production. Its core values—Protect, Engage, Perform—guide a focus on long-term partnerships, supply continuity, and protection of customer tooling investments.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Structural foam injection molding", "In-house tool room and mold maintenance", "Tool transfer and validation", "Large tonnage production", "High-volume injection molding", "Structural foam molding for large components", "Captive operations extrusion", "Plastic fabrication services", "Automated injection molding"], "industries": ["Consumer products", "Office furniture", "Durable goods", "Building materials", "Home improvement", "Kitchen and appliance components", "Electronic housings", "Material handling", "Lawn and garden", "Building and construction", "Plumbing", "Construction", "Cookware", "Safe manufacturing", "Medical products"], "materials": ["HDPE", "Polypropylene", "Elastomer"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house tool room with direct control over mold build, refurbishment, and maintenance", "Structural foam molding for thick-wall components (0.200\u20130.500 in) at production scale", "Managed tool transfers with validation and startup in as little as one weekend", "Nearly 90 injection molding machines operating 24/7", "Dedicated project engineer for each program from quote through production"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1953 in Harborcreek, Pennsylvania -> db", "Family-owned and engineering-driven -> home page", "Nearly 90 injection molding machines operating 24/7 -> home page", "In-house tool room for mold build, refurbishment, and maintenance -> home page", "Structural foam molding for wall thicknesses 0.200\u20130.500 inches, parts up to 7.5 feet -> home page", "Industries served: consumer products, office furniture, durable goods, building materials, home improvement, kitchen/appliance components, electronic housings, material handling, lawn and garden, building and construction -> home page", "Case study: structural foam redesign reduced cycle time 40% and part weight 20% for HDPE trench drains -> home page", "Case study: medical product mold transfer stabilized in one weekend -> home page", "Core values: Protect, Engage, Perform -> home page", "Materials: HDPE, polypropylene, elastomer -> home page"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in custom plastic molding and structural foam molding engineered to support large components with sustained high-volume production.", "founded_year": "1953", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='port-erie-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Reading, Pennsylvania, Poward Plastics has been producing custom plastic injection molded parts for over 50 years. The company is family-owned and operated across multiple generations, with materials sourced from U.S. suppliers and all manufacturing completed domestically.

The shop runs injection molding presses from 25 to 120 tons in-house and partners with facilities up to 6,000 tons, with a maximum press size of 1,400 tons. It produces parts up to 78.7 × 59 × 31.5 inches, holding tolerances of ±0.002 inch. Services include insert molding, overmolding, prototype and production tooling (aluminum and P20 steel), multi-cavity and family molds, mold building, repair, and maintenance, as well as 3D printing and CNC modeling for prototyping. Minimum orders start at 100 parts with a $5,000 threshold.

Customers span medical (valves, syringes, bushings), automotive (plugs, fittings), electronics (housings, accessories), aerospace and defense (ITAR-registered), food and beverage, packaging and displays, industrial, and government sectors. The company ships nationwide and offers free local delivery in the Reading area.

Poward Plastics emphasizes domestic sourcing and production, mold storage and warehousing for reorders, and experience transferring tooling from offshore manufacturers. It holds ITAR and RoHS certifications and provides design engineering assistance, rapid tooling in two weeks, and production tooling in three weeks.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Molding", "Insert Molding", "Overmolding", "Prototype Molding", "Production Tooling (P20 steel)", "Rapid Tooling (aluminum)", "Multi-cavity Molds", "Family Molds", "Mold Building", "Mold Repair", "Mold Maintenance", "Product Design and Engineering", "3D Printing", "CNC Modeling", "Warehousing and Mold Storage", "Design for Manufacturability Review", "First Article Inspection (T1 samples)", "Pad Printing", "Ultrasonic Welding", "Silk Screening", "Painting", "Light Assembly", "Protective Packaging"], "industries": ["Medical", "Automotive", "Electronics", "Aerospace & Defense", "Food & Beverage", "Packaging & Displays", "Industrial", "Government"], "materials": ["ABS", "Nylon (PA 6)", "Polyethylene (PE)", "Polypropylene (PP)", "Polycarbonate (PC)", "High Density Polyethylene (HDPE)", "Low Density Polyethylene (LDPE)", "Polystyrene (PS)", "Polyvinyl chloride (PVC)", "PEEK", "POM (Acetal/Delrin)", "Polyethylene Terephthalate (PET)", "Thermoplastic Elastomer (TPE)", "Polycarbonate/ABS (PC/ABS)", "Polyurethane (PU)", "Polymethyl Methacrylate (PMMA/Acrylic)", "Carbon fibers", "Glass fibers", "UV absorbers", "Flame retardants", "Plasticizers", "Colorants"], "equipment": ["Injection molding presses (25-120 ton in-house)", "Injection molding presses (up to 6,000 ton via network)", "1,400-ton maximum press"], "volume": "100 parts to high-volume production runs", "lead_time": "As low as 2 weeks for T1 samples; after approval, <10,000 parts as low as 1 week", "tolerances": "\u00b10.002 in (\u00b10.05 mm)", "built_on": ["USA-sourced materials and domestic production", "Family-owned across multiple generations", "Mold storage and warehousing for reorders", "Free local delivery in Reading, PA area", "Experience transferring molds from offshore"], "facts_used": ["Based in Reading, PA -> /", "Family-owned for multiple generations -> /", "Over 50 years of operation -> /", "Materials sourced in USA, parts made in America -> /", "Injection molding capacities 25-120 tons in-house -> /services", "Network facilities up to 6000 tons -> /services", "Max press size 1400T -> /capabilities", "Max part size 2000x1500x800 mm -> /capabilities", "Tolerance \u00b10.002 in -> /capabilities", "Lead time 2 weeks for T1 samples -> /capabilities", "Lead time <10k parts as low as 1 week -> /capabilities", "Min order 100 parts and $5000 -> /capabilities", "Certifications: ITAR, RoHS -> / and db", "Industries: medical, automotive, electronics, aerospace/defense, food/beverage, packaging/displays, industrial, government -> / and /services", "Free local delivery in Reading area -> /", "Mold storage and warehousing for reorders -> /", "Experience transferring molds from offshore -> /services", "Rapid tooling in 2 weeks, production tooling in 3 weeks -> /capabilities", "Materials list -> /capabilities", "Insert molding, overmolding, multi-cavity, family molds -> /capabilities", "3D printing and CNC modeling for prototypes -> /services", "Design engineering assistance -> /", "Nationwide delivery -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Poward Plastics is a leading American manufacturer of high-quality plastic injection molded products and services.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "100 parts and $5000", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='poward-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Power Plus is headquartered in Anaheim, California, and was founded in 1987 by Steve Bray. Bray, a former electrician working on Southern California construction sites, recognized that contractors needed more than equipment—they needed reliable problem-solvers. The company began as a small temporary power operation in Orange County.

Today, Power Plus operates nationwide with 500–999 employees and describes itself as the largest independent power solutions provider in America. Services span utility infrastructure, permanent electrical installation, and portable equipment sales.

The company serves construction, oil and gas, mining, disaster response, agriculture, healthcare, data centers, retail distribution, commercial facilities, critical infrastructure, and telecommunications. Its customer base includes Amazon, Walmart, Costco, and roughly half of the Fortune 100. In the 1990s, Power Plus supplied power for global entertainment productions such as the Rolling Stones tour, Olympic events, and the Super Bowl.

Power Plus emphasizes a problem-solving culture: technicians walk sites, listen to requirements, and design custom solutions rather than offering cookie-cutter packages. The firm maintained a no-layoff policy during the COVID-19 pandemic, reflecting a people-first philosophy rooted in Bray’s original vision of doing whatever it takes to deliver power whenever and wherever it is needed.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Generator rental", "Generator service and maintenance", "Temporary power system design and installation", "Power distribution switchgear (ATS, transformers)", "Backup power system installation", "Fuel management", "Designed video surveillance (DVS)", "100% U.S.-based live monitoring", "Utility infrastructure construction", "Permanent electrical installation", "Portable equipment sales", "Disaster response power deployment", "Construction site temporary power", "Critical power solutions for healthcare and data centers", "Remote site power delivery"], "industries": ["Construction", "Oil & gas", "Mining", "Disaster response", "Agriculture", "Healthcare", "Data centers", "Retail distribution", "Commercial facilities", "Critical infrastructure", "Entertainment", "Telecommunications"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Generators", "Temporary power switchgear", "Automatic transfer switches (ATS)", "Transformers", "Portable power equipment", "Video surveillance systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest independent power solutions provider in America", "Nationwide 24/7 operations with four integrated service divisions", "Problem-solving culture: site walks, custom designs, no cookie-cutter solutions", "People-first philosophy: no layoffs during COVID-19", "100% U.S.-based live monitoring for video surveillance"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Anaheim, California -> db", "Founded: 1987 -> db", "Founder: Steve Bray -> /about-us", "Employee count: 500-999 -> db", "Largest independent power solutions provider in America -> /about-us", "Four core divisions: Construction Services, Portable Power Solutions, Critical Power Solutions, Designed Video Surveillance -> /about-us", "Services: generator rental, temporary power switchgear, ATS, transformers, backup power installs, fuel management, DVS, live monitoring -> /about-us and /", "Industries served: construction, oil & gas, mining, disaster response, agriculture -> db", "Additional industries: healthcare, data centers, retail distribution, commercial facilities, critical infrastructure, entertainment, telecommunications -> /about-us", "Customers: Amazon, Walmart, Costco, half of Fortune 100 -> /about-us", "Historical projects: Rolling Stones tour, Olympic events, Super Bowl -> /about-us", "Problem-solving culture: site walks, custom solutions -> /about-us", "No layoffs during COVID-19 -> /about-us", "24/7 operation -> /", "4-hour emergency response for freezers -> /", "Disney residential project 2-mile 12kV line -> /", "Hospital power during Cat 4 hurricane -> /", "Remote telecom site on volcano in Hawaii -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Power Plus is a California power solutions provider focused on rental and turnkey power systems.", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "500-999", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='power-plus' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Power Trans Inc. was established in 1967 in Bridgeville, Delaware, as a distributor of power transmission components and industrial supplies. The company maintains its headquarters on Fawn Road in Bridgeville and operates a second branch in Bear, Delaware, serving the Mid-Atlantic region.

The business distributes a range of power transmission products from manufacturers such as Carlisle, Daido, Rexnord, Browning, Lovejoy, Morse, Sealmaster, and 4B Components Limited.

The company positions its value on long-standing relationships with both suppliers and end users, leveraging decades of product knowledge to address production and process challenges.

The firm emphasizes quality customer relationships and access to superior brands as its primary differentiators, with a team that offers experience and technical knowledge to keep client operations running efficiently.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Power transmission component distribution", "Industrial supply distribution", "Conveyor component supply", "Hydraulic hose assembly supply", "4B Components Limited product distribution", "Technical product support"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1967 -> db", "Headquarters Bridgeville, DE -> db and /about", "Distributor of power transmission components -> /about", "Brands carried: Carlisle, Daido, Rexnord, Browning, Lovejoy, Morse, Sealmaster, 4B Components, JAX Lubricants -> /", "Two locations: Bridgeville and Bear, DE -> /", "Conveyor components and hydraulic hose assemblies offered -> /", "Emphasis on customer relationships and experienced sales staff -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Power Trans Inc. has served as a distributor of power transmission components and industrial supply since 1967.", "founded_year": "1967", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='power-trans-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Precise Connections, Inc. has operated from Duncanville, Texas, since 1985.

The company provides end-to-end electronics manufacturing services, including PCB assembly (through-hole, surface-mount, and mixed-technology), custom box builds, cable and wire harness assembly, design-for-manufacturing consultation, functional testing, and supply-chain management. Prototypes and full production runs share the same floor, supported by an Aptean Made2Manage ERP system with Panasonic PanaCIM lot traceability and RFID-tracked inventory. The facility maintains a fully ESD-controlled environment with calibrated test equipment and a formal corrective-action process.

Precise serves OEMs across regulated and performance-critical markets such as energy storage, medical devices, industrial equipment, printing, audio, marine and marine audio, safety devices, railway, control systems, motion detection, IT and networking, and consumer products. The company also supports OEM programs and aftermarket service. Components are sourced globally through authorized distributors and factory-direct channels, with broker assistance for hard-to-find parts.

The firm emphasizes a single-point-of-contact model from design handoff through fulfillment, describing itself as "big enough to deliver, small enough to be agile." Its quality system is certified to ISO 9001:2015 and compliant with IPC-A-610 and IPC/WHMA-A-620 up to Class III, with RoHS 2 adherence across all processes. In 2025, customer ratings earned Precise the Circuits Assembly Service Excellence Award for Responsiveness among EMS providers under $20 million in sales. The company cites 30 consecutive profitable quarters and a staff averaging more than ten years of industry experience as indicators of stability.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IPC-A-610','IPC/WHMA-A-620','RoHS 2']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Assembly (Through-hole, SMT, Mixed-technology)", "Custom Box Builds", "Cable & Wire Assembly", "Design Consultation (DFM)", "Functional Testing", "Supply Chain Management", "Component Sourcing", "Inventory Management (RFID)", "ERP Lot Traceability (Aptean Made2Manage, Panasonic PanaCIM)", "ESD-Controlled Manufacturing", "Calibration Management", "First-Article Inspection", "Corrective Action Process"], "industries": ["Energy storage", "Medical devices", "Industrial", "Printing", "Audio", "Marine & marine audio", "Safety devices", "Railway", "Control", "Motion detection", "IT & networking", "Consumer products", "OEM programs & aftermarket support"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Aptean Made2Manage ERP", "Panasonic PanaCIM", "RFID inventory tracking"], "volume": "Prototype to full production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end manufacturing under one roof with a single point of contact", "Consigned to turnkey flexibility \u2013 prototype and production on the same floor", "39,000 sq ft Duncanville facility, 30 minutes to DFW airport and four hours to Port of Houston", "Global component sourcing with US-based assembly, test, and shipment", "ISO 9001:2015 certified, IPC-A-610/WHMA-A-620 Class III compliant, RoHS 2"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1985 -> /about", "Headquarters Duncanville, Texas -> /, /about", "39,000 sq ft across two adjacent buildings -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /about", "IPC-A-610 and IPC/WHMA-A-620 workmanship standards -> /, /about", "RoHS 2 compliant -> /about", "Industries served: energy storage, medical devices, industrial, printing, audio, marine & marine audio, safety devices, railway, control, motion detection, IT & networking, consumer products, OEM programs & aftermarket support -> /about", "PCB assembly: through-hole, SMT, mixed-technology -> /", "Custom box builds -> /", "Cable & wire assembly -> /", "Design consultation (DFM) -> /", "Testing and troubleshooting -> /", "Supply chain solutions -> /", "Global sourcing, US assembly -> /", "30 consecutive profitable quarters -> /about", "Staff averaging 10+ years experience -> /about", "2025 Circuits Assembly Service Excellence Award for Responsiveness -> /, /about", "Aptean Made2Manage ERP, Panasonic PanaCIM -> /about", "RFID-tracked inventory -> /about", "ESD-controlled facility -> /about", "Calibration program -> /about", "First-article inspection, CAR process -> /about", "Prototype to full production volumes -> /", "Consigned to turnkey -> /", "30 minutes to DFW, four hours to Port of Houston -> /", "Right-to-work state -> /", "Distributors like Mouser down the road -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Texas-based electronics contract manufacturing", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='precise-connections-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Precision Inc., a TT Electronics Company, is headquartered in Brooklyn Center, Minnesota.

Precision Inc. designs and manufactures electronic solutions for performance-critical applications. Its capabilities span precision sensors, passive components, rugged power conversion, complex electronics assemblies, custom cable harness assemblies, optoelectronics components, and transformers. The vertically integrated model covers design through manufacturing, serving regulated markets with high-reliability electronics.

The company serves OEMs in aerospace and defence, healthcare, and automation and electrification. Concrete customer engagements include a Global Supplier Framework Agreement with Wabtec Corporation for transit, freight, and signalling; an extended partnership with Rolls-Royce for future aircraft power; work with MBDA Italia; and Optek Hall-effect sensors selected for NASA''s Dragonfly mission fan assemblies.

TT Electronics states its purpose is to engineer and manufacture electronic solutions enabling a safer, healthier, and more sustainable world. The focus on regulated, high-reliability markets drives investment in vertical integration and design-led manufacturing to reduce programme risk before qualification begins.', certifications=ARRAY['MIL-STD']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision sensors", "Passive components", "Rugged power conversion", "Complex electronics assemblies", "Custom cable harness assembly", "Optoelectronics components", "Transformer design and manufacturing", "Vertical integration (design through manufacturing)", "High-reliability electronics manufacturing"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defence", "Healthcare", "Automation & Electrification", "Transit, Freight & Signalling", "Space"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated design and manufacturing", "Design-led advanced electronics for performance-critical applications", "Global footprint with 20 facilities in UK, North America, and Asia", "Brand portfolio including Optek Technologies, AB Connectors, and IRC", "Trusted partner to OEMs in regulated markets worldwide"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Brooklyn Center, Minnesota -> db", "Part of TT Electronics PLC, evolved over 100 years with brands AB Connectors, Aero Stanrew, BI Technologies, IRC, Optek Technologies -> /about", "3,500+ employees, 20 locations, \u00a3481.4M revenue -> /about", "Vertically integrated design and manufacturing -> /", "Capabilities: precision sensors, passive components, rugged power conversion, complex electronics assemblies, custom cable harness, optoelectronics, transformers -> /, /about", "Core markets: Healthcare, Aerospace & Defence, Automation & Electrification -> /about", "Customers: Wabtec, Rolls-Royce, MBDA Italia, NASA Dragonfly mission -> /", "Purpose: engineer and manufacture electronic solutions enabling a safer, healthier, more sustainable world -> /about", "Certification: MIL-STD -> db", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "At TT Electronics, we engineer and manufacture solutions that enable a safer, healthier and more sustainable world. From precision sensors and passive components to rugged power conversion and complex electronics assemblies, we are a trusted partner to OEMs in regulated markets worldwide.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "3500+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/tt-electronics-plc/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='precision-inc-a-tt-electronics-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
